       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/kw738fg7467.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "Four pencil figures on crop 1, written right at the top edge of the paper so the upper part of each is clipped; read from the lower, upright panel and cross-checked against the rotated one. Separators dropped, so 8.6.22. The first figure is the open-loop form that can be taken for a 6, but it crosses at the waist and the second figure, a plain 6 beside it, has no such crossing, so I read 8 then 6; if the first were a 6 the date would be 6.6.22. Roll number 2588 written in pencil on crop 4, from a different part of the roll than the date. Crop 3 carries a later English note, 'Finish of Funeral March.', with a long rule; crop 2 has pencil clipped away almost entirely at the paper edge, crop 5 is blank."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
